  "text": "Recipe: Chinese Gnocchi in Mushroom Sauce\nCreator: Frank Lee\nCategory: Main Dish\nIngredients: shiitake mushroom, chestnuts, preserved radish, spring onion, garlic, low sodium soy sauce, vegetable bouillon, potatoes, potato starch\nCooking methods: saute, steam, boil, no-cook\nInstructions: MUSHROOM SAUCE: Mix 1/2 cup shiitake mushroom (soaked and chopped), 1/2 cup chestnuts chopped, 1/2 cup preserved radish chopped, 1/2 cup spring onion chopped, 1 clove garlic diced, 1 Tbsp low sodium soy sauce, vegetable bouillon. Sauté for 2 mins.\nGNOCCHI: Mix 2 potatoes (steamed & mashed) with 1/2 cup potato starch. Form gnocchi balls & shape them using bottle (see pic). Boil these balls and set them aside.\nMIX & SERVE: Mix cooked gnocchi & mushroom sauce well. Garnish with chopped spring onion.\nNotes: A recipe with TUBERS (potato, potato starch), MUSHROOMS (shiitake), RAINBOW VEGGIES (chestnuts, radish, spring onion), HERBS & SPICES (various), MISC (vegetable bouillon).\nShared in FaceBook Group: \"SANE (Sleep, Attitude, Nutrition, Exercise) for Life\"\nAPPAM PAN",
